 "why_it_matters": "The realizer replaces a width-4 beam whose per-attempt cost was bounded and small.  A complete search costs more per attempt, so a bind-rate gain could be swamped by attempts the lane no longer has time to make.  This is measured rather than inferred, because the two cost distributions overlap in the wrong direction: the UNPRODUCTIVE searches are the expensive ones."
